 "summary": "Implemented and pushed as draft PR #11729 (Part of #11693). The console keeps the `timezone` that GET /api/v1/auth/me/localization answers. LocalizationValue carries it, and LocalizationProvider hands it to a new display zone in @object-ui/core date-display (setDisplayTimeZone / getDisplayTimeZone / subscribeDisplayTimeZone). Every date and datetime face reads that zone for instants. A date-only value keeps its day: toDisplayDate registers the calendar-day Dates it builds, so the exemption survives hand-offs such as GridField's date cell. With no zone, every face is unchanged. Measurement moved the landing point from the dispatch's i18n formatters: every console datetime call site renders through core's date-display, threading only { locale }, while i18n formatting.ts and formatDateSpec (which already takes a timeZone) have no caller outside @object-ui/i18n. Zone 2 hypothesis 3 is falsified as a route. The core premise holds (the fetch did drop timezone), but two sub-premises do not. First, the served zone is the WORKSPACE default (localization.timezone; sys_user has no zone, and per-user overrides are out of scope for v1). Second, the wire never says 'none': the cascade floors timezone to UTC. Status needs_decision because the merge is gated on that floor. Merged alone, this PR moves every unconfigured workspace's datetimes from the viewer's zone to UTC. The PR is complete and identical under options A, B and D (D adds one line). It opens with 'Part of #11693' so that merging does not close the card before the ruling; under B, the seat closes the card after the merge.",
 "tests": "All cited at HEAD 229db2b. Final union: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/core/ packages/i18n/ apps/console/src/LocalizationFetchProvider.test.tsx apps/console/src/__tests__/localizationBootDedup.test.tsx` gave 'Test Files 281 passed (281) / Tests 5257 passed | 40 skipped' (VERDICT command-exit 0). This includes date-display.dateOnlyZone-10110, whose real TZ=America/Los_Angeles and TZ=Asia/Shanghai children measure the rewritten relative-day arithmetic unchanged. New pins: core date-display.displayZone-11693 (16), i18n LocalizationContext.timezone-11693 (5), console LocalizationFetchProvider (2 new; 14 in the file). Los_Angeles set: 2026-09-02T03:00Z renders 'Sep 1, 2026, 08:00 PM'. None set: 'Sep 2, 2026, 03:00 AM'. A date-only 2026-09-01 renders 'Sep 1' on every face under the west zone. Control: the same instant as a plain Date renders 'Aug 31'. Consumers: 168 files (every mount of LocalizationProvider or LocalizationFetchProvider, plus the date and datetime suites of fields, components, plugin-grid, plugin-gantt, plugin-dashboard and others) gave '82 passed | 2 skipped' and '83 passed | 1 skipped', 0 failed. type-check: @object-ui/core and @object-ui/i18n exit 0. The console type-check was narrowed: the two touched console files and the two README snippets compile with the console tsconfig against built core, i18n and auth, exit 0. Reverse check: a misspelt key gives TS2353. Ablations via ablation-replace.mjs, each restored with blob == HEAD and git diff HEAD empty: (1) console drops timezone: 1 failed / 13 passed. (2) toDisplayDate stops registering: 4 failed / 12 passed, reading 'Aug 31' / 'Yesterday'. (3) toInclusiveEndDay stops registering: 1 failed / 15 passed. (4) default datetime face takes no zone: 4 failed / 17 passed. Its first attempt was refused by the tool and was a no-op, because the replacement was a substring of the anchor; it was rerun with a marker. (5) provider does not hand the zone to core: 4 failed / 15 passed. (6) context keyed on the prop zone (the ordering hazard): 3 failed / 2 passed, showing 'America/Los_Angeles|Sep 2, 2026, 03:00 AM'. (7) i18n hands setDisplayTimeZone a number: TS2345, so the type-check reads core's rebuilt d.ts. Rebuilds: the core closure (types, core), then i18n, auth and its closure, before any type judgement.",
