 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "The served timezone floors to UTC for a workspace that configured none (objectstack resolveCurrentUserLocalization: 'Always a string — the cascade's floor is UTC', pinned by a test; the settings row is 'Default timezone', default 'UTC', described as governing 'rendered datetimes'). The card wants 'with none set, it renders in the browser's', and the wire can never say none. Merged alone, PR #11729 moves every unconfigured workspace's datetimes from the viewer's zone to UTC. Which contract holds?",
   "options": [
    "A — the server says none: the endpoint answers timezone null when only the default answered (the settings service reports source 'default'). Server TODAY() and buckets keep the UTC floor, and unconfigured workspaces keep the viewer's zone. Cost: an objectstack change that reverses the endpoint's pinned 'never null' for timezone, plus its tests. Client: #11729 unchanged.",
    "B — keep the floor: the configured-or-default zone governs rendered datetimes, as the settings row already declares. Display, TODAY() and analytics buckets share one zone. Cost: unconfigured workspaces render in UTC until an admin sets the zone. Client: #11729 unchanged; it completes the card.",
    "C — the client reads 'UTC' as unset: refused. A workspace that really chose UTC renders in the viewer's zone, and it is consumer-side tolerance (objectui AGENTS.md #0.1, os-dev rule 5).",
    "D — a separate wire signal (for example timezoneSource): additive. Cost: one more field on the wire, an objectstack change, and one line in the console fetch provider."
   ],
   "recommendation": "B. Real business need: the only measured declaration (the settings row's description) says this zone governs rendered datetimes. Who configures it in practice is not measurable from here, and B's cost lands exactly on unconfigured workspaces, which is A's argument. Long-run fit: B leaves one reference zone for display, TODAY() and buckets, the Salesforce default-time-zone shape the locale ruling invoked. A keeps a client-only second zone that server-side features cannot follow. AI error-proofing: B has one declared meaning and no 'null means the browser' rule for an author or a server-side renderer to miss. Startup focus: B needs no further work; A and D need a server change and a wire or contract change. If UTC display on unconfigured workspaces is unacceptable, the lever is the default (provisioning sets localization.timezone, or the manifest's default), not a client fallback; that is a separate decision. Choose A if the unconfigured workspace's experience outweighs one shared zone."
  }
 ],
